is a halfling kitchen worker and rogue played by Jasmine Don in Exandria Unlimited: Divergence.

Fiedra was small for a halfling, scrawny, wiry, and tough-looking, with red hair worn in two pigtails. She had a tattoo of a cockroach on her shoulder. When first seen, she looked as though she hadn't been sleeping well recently.

Fiedra grew up orphaned in a city, and at some point became the leader of a gang there. At around age 13, she acquired a "dragon egg" (winning it in a game of cards), and when it hatched into Crokas, she raised him. When Crokas was ten or eleven, they were both captured and brought to Rybad-Kol, where Fiedra worked in its kitchen, the Slop, gaining some amount of control there, and the trust of at least one of the guards. Crokas acted as a bodyguard to Fiedra. They worked in the kitchen for four or five years, and with several other workers formed their own gang, the Roaches..}}

Halandil "Hal" Fang is an orc bard played by Liam O'Brien in Campaign Four.

Hal is an older orcish gentleman with white-streaked dark hair, who wears fine but not ostentatious clothing. He has smile lines around his eyes "from a life well-lived". Halandil is 6'2" tall. Nov 2025|12:24}}

Hal has tried to maintain a buoyant spirit throughout his life., where even as a 19-year-old he wore a smile most of the time although there was worry behind his eyes.}} Liam O'Brien described him as: "Hal is a successful entrepreneur of the arts, and family man, and scion of the city of Dol-Makjar. He's very much a man concerned with history and the future and finding the mortal identity in this godless world. Hal's real danger spot is his children. If someone really wanted to hurt Hal, it would be to go for his kids." His life has been full of family, friends, art, meaning and purpose, and a successful business. Nov 2025|05:52}}

Halandil grew up in the Rookery as the son of a foreign emissary and a soldier who separated when he was young. His mother, as an emissary, got him books from far away lands, so Hal grew up as a well-learned child. He was close to Thjazi Fang, his paternal younger half-brother, although they didn't see eye to eye all the time. Hal had to reprimand Thjazi from time to time, and Thjazi "gave him shit" when he was ten, but eventually the dynamic became more respectful. Later in life Thjazi started hiding dangerous aspects of his life from Hal to protect him..}}

is a pixie rogue played by Laura Bailey in Campaign Four.

Thimble is a four-inch-tall pixie, who appears to be about 18 years old. She has short brown hair (with a single short braid to honor Teor Pridesire), sparkly freckles, and ordinarily has spring-green wings, with eyes of that same color. She wears dark green clothing and a large button at her waist, has an industrial piercing in her right ear, and carries two needles as swords. She smells like honeysuckle, and the scent feels effervescent and otherworldly. The pixie dust on her usually gives her a spring-green golden glow, although the color and intensity of the glow can change depending of the situation,, where Brennan described how the presence of a lot of cold iron and symbols of the Candescent Creed in Tybry's Lea made Thimble's light diminish.}} and she can suppress it completely, if she so wishes.

Thimble is a stone cold killer with a history, and the kind of person who'd start a bar fight. She's a warrior pixie, and a badass who doesn't take any shit. Campaign 4 Ep 1-4 Recap]"| vod=https://youtu.be/hdLPwuKMlIY | 11:52}}

She cares deeply for her close friends, evident when she broke down into tears having heard she failed to save Thjazi. Her priority now is trying to make it right by causing suffering to anybody that did that to him. She believes that if she finishes what Thjazi started, "maybe then I'll feel better." Campaign 4 Ep 1-4 Recap]" | vod=https://youtu.be/hdLPwuKMlIY | 12:32}}

is an elven paladin played by Ashley Johnson in Campaign Four.

Vaelus is extremely tall, and she has lavender skin with visible facial scarring of magical origin that spread across her body (with their origin being something the elf prefers not to explain outloud). Episode 2 Discussing Up To C4E18|48:41}} Episode 2 Discussing Up To C4E18|1:21:58}} She dresses in deep obsidian, including snug black leather chest armor and robes, with a black hood and pale white lace that goes to the top of her throat. She carries a long chain with a bladed censer that emits smoke. She wears a veil of mourning that appears to be made of chainmail. Ashley Johnson described her as a "nun assassin". Campaign 4 Ep 1-4 Recap]" | vod=https://youtu.be/hdLPwuKMlIY | 14:19}}

Vaelus has a cold and calm demeanor. She was driven by her goal to find the Stone of Nightsong but she could show patience in order to obtain what she wanted. Finding and protecting every relic of Sylandri is very important to her. The feelings that she has for the lost goddess are what drives her. She is drawn to Occtis's magic because he has returned from the dead. Campaign 4 Ep 1-4 Recap]" | vod=https://youtu.be/hdLPwuKMlIY | 15:07}} She generally struggles trusting other people. Episode 2 Discussing Up To C4E18|18:48}}

Vaelus was once a very happy and joyful elf who spent her time in celebrations and activities with her family, honoring their creator goddess, Sylandri. Only a few years before her 50th birthday she was somewhat conflicted about finding her purpose honoring the Green Mother, since she was devout but couldn't remember the prayers, and found more enjoyment in climbing trees than in trying to memorize them. In the Shapers' War, seventy years before Campaign Four, Vaelus watched the death of the last of the Shapers; when the Last Arrow was shot, her sister Maywyn was nearby and was distracted by the light of the weapon, causing her to be killed by a battleaxe in front of Vaelus. Afterwards, she spent decades of mourning and prayer with the Sisters of Sylandri, occasionally fighting the undead alongside them. About a decade before the war Vaelus had traveled across Pasitar at least once, and did so again when she was a Sister of Sylandri briefly visiting the Eternal Night before and after its creation. In her journeys she learned about the other Shapers out of curiosity.

was an actress who worked with Halandil Fang, and for whom Wicander Halovar felt a romantic attachment..}}

Wicander met Armas through their mutual connection Halandil Fang, when she was an actress in Hal's troupe and Wicander was taking lessons from him. Wicander attended her performances and (according to Tyranny) spent the following hours praying a lot. According to Wick part of their connection was due to the nature of theater itself, and he denied that she was his girlfriend, although they "felt a bit of a connection". Wicander kept a portrait of her in his room, which was one of the few things he took with him when he ran away from his family. Following their first mission together, Wicander told Tyranny that he was feeling vulnerable around her, and it made him really realize that he missed Armas very much, and he should search for her.

Armas had gone missing at about the same time Wicander's family arranged his betrothal to wealthy heiress Ebecca D'Antonio..}} His family was aware of the relationship as a romance, and Yanessa described the girl as "the one who got away", when reminding her grandson that he would have to marry Ebecca anyway.
